| Router Type             | What It Does                                                                  | Common Use                        |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| **Home Router**         | Connects devices on a home network to the internet                            | Homes, apartments                 |
| **SOHO Router**         | Small-office/home-office router with more business features                   | Small businesses, home offices    |
| **Enterprise Router**   | Handles large amounts of network traffic and complex routing                  | Large companies                   |
| **Core Router**         | Moves massive amounts of traffic between major parts of a network             | ISPs, data centers                |
| **Edge Router**         | Connects an organization's network to an outside network                      | Businesses, ISPs                  |
| **Distribution Router** | Connects different network segments and aggregates traffic                    | Enterprise networks               |
| **Wireless Router**     | Combines routing with Wi-Fi access                                            | Homes, offices                    |
| **Virtual Router**      | Router implemented as software rather than dedicated hardware                 | Cloud/data centers                |
| **Cloud Router**        | Provides routing between cloud networks and other networks                    | AWS, Azure, Google Cloud          |
| **VPN Router**          | Routes traffic through VPN tunnels and can provide secure remote connectivity | Businesses, remote workers        |
| **Cellular Router**     | Uses cellular networks such as 4G/5G instead of wired internet                | Remote locations, mobile networks |
| **Modular Router**      | Allows network interfaces/modules to be added or replaced                     | Enterprise/ISP networks           |
| **Multiservice Router** | Handles routing plus services such as voice, video, VPN, and security         | Enterprise networks               |
| **Software Router**     | Uses a computer/server and routing software to perform routing                | Labs, servers, virtualization     |
| **BGP Router**          | Uses BGP to exchange routing information between autonomous systems           | ISPs, large organizations         |
| **NAT Router**          | Translates private IP addresses into public IP addresses                      | Homes and businesses              |

